From a035679500cef2b3563bdddfd0b8fb65bbb0e684 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:03:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: an I2C scan gives up after one second

Why: scan_i2c probes up to 117 addresses, one read each, with no limit
on the total time. On a stuck bus (SDA held low) every address costs one
adapter timeout, and which errno a stuck address gives differs by
adapter (bcm2835, RP1 designware, i2c-gpio). The scan is about to run
under the command lock, so an unbounded scan would hold every other
command. Original Apertar bounds a wait with a steady_clock deadline,
as waitForTimedatectlNetworkSync does.

What: the scan sets a deadline of one second before the address loop.
After each probe it checks the deadline; once passed, it refuses with
"I2C bus N does not answer: check the wiring." A healthy bus finishes
well inside the bound. I2cProbe.cpp is unchanged.

Tested: check_core.sh both tests (PASS, no new warnings). --simulate:
scan_i2c bus=1 still answers "Bus 1 does not exist on this Pi." and a
missing bus still gets its sentence. Needs the camera, on Pi 4, Pi 5/CM5
and CM4: time python3 ~/apertar-kb/working/tools/core.py scan_i2c bus=1
lists the same addresses as i2cdetect -y -r 1 and takes well under 1 s.
Optional bench check: SDA (GPIO 2) to GND through 1 kOhm; the scan
returns the sentence within about 1 s plus one adapter timeout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp b/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
index ec86c8b..a7d571e 100644
--- a/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
+++ b/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
@@ -12524,6 +12524,7 @@ std::optional<std::string> ApertarCoreApp::handleReadOnlyHardwareCommand(const C
         std::ostringstream body;
         body << "\"bus\":" << bus << ",\"found\":[";
         bool first = true;
+        const auto deadline = std::chrono::steady_clock::now() + std::chrono::seconds(1);
         for (int address = 0x03; address <= 0x77; ++address) {
             const auto guess = known.find(address);
             std::string by;
@@ -12533,6 +12534,8 @@ std::optional<std::string> ApertarCoreApp::handleReadOnlyHardwareCommand(const C
                 const hardware::I2cProbe probe = hardware::probeI2cAddress(bus, address);
                 if (!probe.busExists)
                     return errorReply(command.id, probe.error.empty() ? "No I2C bus " + std::to_string(bus) + "." : probe.error);
+                if (std::chrono::steady_clock::now() >= deadline)
+                    return errorReply(command.id, "I2C bus " + std::to_string(bus) + " does not answer: check the wiring.");
                 if (!probe.found)
                     continue;
                 by = probe.kernelDriver ? "kernel" : "";
